                    {
                        "form_id": "8a652b51-ef62-459d-9419-2abe000fd074",
                        "entry_id": "14a3d941-b67a-3f5a-bbc2-0957b74e2f60",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "maelström"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4397613-a5ba-3fa1-990f-16c7f3757ff5",
                        "entry_id": "14a3d941-b67a-3f5a-bbc2-0957b74e2f60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fort remous circulaire dans un fluide, tourbillon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ef70f2d-f345-4bdf-b52c-50fce50c7b91",
                                "sense_id": "b4397613-a5ba-3fa1-990f-16c7f3757ff5",
                                "text": "Moi qui tremblais, sentant geindre à cinquante lieues\nLe rut des Béhémots et les Maelstroms épais,\nFileur éternel des immobilités bleues,\nJe regrette l’Europe aux anciens parapets !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31f790ab-93b3-3505-b51a-410e04dda72c",
                        "entry_id": "14a3d941-b67a-3f5a-bbc2-0957b74e2f60",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mouvement impétueux d'agitation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1dcd8759-0f34-43b8-a381-a5ab4e127061",
                                "sense_id": "31f790ab-93b3-3505-b51a-410e04dda72c",
                                "text": "Le boulevard est un maëlstrom de soie et d’or, où viennent se perdre bien des petites naufs qui, sûres de leur mâture et de leurs agrès, riaient du naufrage des autres et ne croyaient pas le leur possible."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10b2f410-9e53-4809-8546-aa7583286d7f",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a3d941-b67a-3f5a-bbc2-0957b74e2f60",
                        "target_lang_word": "maelstrom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "maelstrom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "860d4a67-b0a2-3886-a952-0d061ad5a1aa",
                                        "entry_id": "090d7402-9f0b-33fe-b81f-2cf59778d76c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large and violent whirlpool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d939bff-dda7-4348-843b-82b07db7339d",
                                                "sense_id": "860d4a67-b0a2-3886-a952-0d061ad5a1aa",
                                                "text": "To his right fell a gleaming sheet of water, and below it was a maelstrom, that made one giddy by its terrific gyrations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38dc513c-b954-4a8f-800a-d717fa04fb51",
                                                "sense_id": "860d4a67-b0a2-3886-a952-0d061ad5a1aa",
                                                "text": "The falukah plunged over a waterfall and was almost submerged, was caught again in a maelstrom and went twirling on in the blackness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1e3b733-5111-455c-8116-a6acedbb9a19",
                                                "sense_id": "860d4a67-b0a2-3886-a952-0d061ad5a1aa",
                                                "text": "A hulking shape burst through the doorway and hurtled down the corridor, leaving a maelstrom of air currents in his wake."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                        "entry_id": "090d7402-9f0b-33fe-b81f-2cf59778d76c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A chaotic or turbulent situation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c036151-0922-47ef-870e-de5075e8fc11",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                                "text": "It was of Jean Paul's doing: some single billow in that vast World-Mahlstrom of Humour, with its heaven-kissing coruscations, which is now, alas, all congealed in the frost of death!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "678c1225-4eb2-418c-b380-837fda59c714",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                                "text": "He escaped at last, dizzy from the maelstrom of conflicting emotions that had caught and whirled him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b0e4ec4-86bf-4a57-9cc0-dc0809b40179",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                                "text": "The terminal station, Richmond, is managed by South West Trains, heirs to the London & South Western Railway, and here the District fades into a railway maelstrom, since Richmond is not only on the Waterloo-Reading line but is also the westerly terminus of the London Overground."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be23758a-d77e-48cf-b645-154fdc85d5d2",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                                "text": "Setting our sights back on King's Landing, where the Last War will be waged, makes a lot of sense, even if it does feel a bit anticlimactic after last week's deadly, blustery maelstrom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67e7651c-3c25-4a80-bf74-756ac444e08f",
                                                "sense_id": "ad1d223d-04d0-391e-8bd6-7115c766fe4a",
                                                "text": "Five, he has no idea what else could be out there. For example, if British doctrine was anything like his own, then even at this moment, dozens of British destroyers might be swarming towards him, about to envelop his forces in a maelstrom of torpedoes, and the first thing he'd know about it is when things start exploding! (Well, even more than they already are now.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
